# Anti Double Charge Concern

## Scope
Prevent duplicate payment processing using idempotency keys - same payment request with same idempotency key must not charge customer twice.

## Out of Scope
Fingerprint validation, complex key generation schemes, distributed cache beyond Redis, idempotency windows beyond payment gateway requirements.

# Aftermath target
After completion: UUIDv4 idempotency key generation per payment request, cache of payment results, duplicate request detection with cached result return. No customer charged twice for same payment.

## Definition of Done
[ ] Idempotency key generation: UUIDv4 per payment request
    [ ] Verification: `console.log('TRACE: Idempotency key generated', { key, requestId })` on new payment
    [ ] Test: Generate 100 keys, verify all unique
[ ] Payment result caching: store result with idempotency key
    [ ] Verification: `console.log('TRACE: Payment result cached', { key, result, ttl })` after successful payment
    [ ] Test: Process payment, verify result stored in cache
[ ] Duplicate detection: return cached result for duplicate key
    [ ] Verification: `console.log('TRACE: Duplicate payment detected', { key, cachedResult })` on duplicate
    [ ] Test: Send same payment twice, verify second returns cached result without charging
